1. DEFINITIONS

"Engine" means the MiniEngine game engine, including its source code,
compiled binaries, libraries, runtime components, and modifications or
derivative versions of those components made available under this License.

"Licensor" means Matěj Dušek and any other copyright holders who expressly
license their contributions under this License.

"You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights granted under
this License.

"Game" means a video game or interactive entertainment application developed
using the Engine, where the Engine serves as an underlying development or
runtime technology rather than the principal product being offered.

"Engine Distribution" means distributing the Engine, in original or modified
form, as a standalone engine, reusable game-development framework, SDK,
engine library package, or substantially equivalent product.

"Runtime Components" means portions of the Engine reasonably necessary to
execute a Game, including compiled libraries and supporting files.

2. PERMISSION TO USE

Subject to this License, the Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive copyright license to:

(a) Download, install, and use the Engine for personal, educational, research,
    and commercial purposes.

(b) Study, modify, and create derivative versions of the Engine.

(c) Develop, publish, distribute, and commercially sell Games created using
    the Engine, provided that such Games include visible attribution to
    MiniEngine in accordance with Section 3.

(d) Distribute Runtime Components as part of Games, including commercially
    distributed Games.

(e) Distribute original or modified versions of the Engine without charge,
    subject to Section 4.

(f) Provide paid consulting, development, training, maintenance, and technical
    support services relating to the Engine, provided these services do not
    constitute prohibited commercial Engine Distribution.

No royalties are owed to the Licensor for Games created using the Engine.

3. COMMERCIAL GAMES AND ATTRIBUTION

You may develop and distribute commercial Games using the Engine, including
Games sold for a one-time price, by subscription, or through in-game purchases.

Games may contain compiled Engine Runtime Components required for their
operation.

A Game does not become a prohibited Engine Distribution merely because it
contains Engine Runtime Components, even when the Game is sold commercially.

You retain ownership of Your independently created game code, artwork, audio,
and other original content. This License does not require You to publish the
source code of Your Game.

However, packaging the Engine as a nominal Game, demonstration, launcher, or
other product primarily intended to distribute a reusable engine does not
avoid the restrictions of Section 4.

3.1. ATTRIBUTION REQUIREMENTS

Any Game developed using MiniEngine and publicly distributed, whether free or
commercial, must include the following attribution:

    Made with MiniEngine

The attribution must:

(a) Be displayed in a reasonably accessible location, such as the Game's
    credits, main menu, or an "About" section.

(b) Be clearly visible and readable to users.

(c) Not be deliberately obscured, removed, or misrepresented.

(d) Remain present in distributed versions of the Game.

The attribution does not need to appear during startup, on loading screens, or
during gameplay.

Developers may additionally display the official MiniEngine logo, provided
they do not imply endorsement or official affiliation.

This requirement also applies to Games developed using modified versions of
MiniEngine.

4. RESTRICTIONS ON COMMERCIAL ENGINE DISTRIBUTION

Without separate written permission from the relevant copyright holders,
You may not:

(a) Sell, rent, or license access to the Engine as a standalone product.

(b) Charge a fee for copies of an Engine Distribution, including modified
    versions or forks.

(c) Offer an Engine Distribution as a paid download, subscription, or
    paid-access package.

(d) Bundle an Engine Distribution with another product primarily as a means
    of charging for access to the Engine.

These restrictions do not prohibit selling Games as permitted by Section 3,
or providing genuine development, support, or consulting services as permitted
by Section 2.

You may distribute original or modified Engine Distributions free of charge,
including through public source-code repositories.

A paid Game containing required Runtime Components is not considered a
prohibited Engine Distribution solely because those Runtime Components are
included.

5. REDISTRIBUTION CONDITIONS

When You distribute the Engine or a modified Engine Distribution, You must:

(a) Include a copy of this License.

(b) Preserve existing copyright and attribution notices.

(c) Clearly identify significant modifications You have made.

(d) Distribute the Engine or modified Engine Distribution without charge.

(e) Not claim that Your modified version is the official MiniEngine release
    unless authorized by the project owner.

You are not required to publish Your private Engine modifications. However,
if You choose to distribute a modified Engine Distribution, the distribution
must comply with this License.

